{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jd1e2rgwDqdCDcn6t7xqsH","type":"tool_result","content":"1045\tRun `pose delegate resume <run>` (`--dry-run` previews it; repeating it returns the recorded continuation) to continue with the same agent, captured session, brief digest, sealed commit and reconstructed checkout digest. Every run of an attempt recreates its sealed checkout at the same path under the dispatcher's temporary directory, so the resumed session finds the checkout it worked in; resume from a shell with the same `TMPDIR`. When that directory is still there (an unfinished cleanup, or another process holding the path), resume refuses before it starts: remove the directory, then resume. Resume uses the original attempt and does not spend another attempt quota. The default maximum is three resumes and 60 minutes of accumulated wall-clock; configure `resume.max_resumes`/`max_wall_time` to change these bounds. Policy changes, changed inputs, lost or rewritten predecessors, terminal predecessors and spent budgets refuse. An immutable predecessor claim permits only one continuation; repeated requests return the recorded result or expose its pending reservation without launching another process. A lost host before a result is published remains explicit incomplete evidence; this is not automatic recovery without a captured interrupted record."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"2caacbbb-7e4e-4235-bc76-7bcf6ec4a3ff","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:19:22.778Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-ed41371fa91497af9df96f254af372d5/worktree/POSE.md","content":"Run `pose delegate resume <run>` (`--dry-run` previews it; repeating it returns the recorded continuation) to continue with the same agent, captured session, brief digest, sealed commit and reconstructed checkout digest. Every run of an attempt recreates its sealed checkout at the same path under the dispatcher's temporary directory, so the resumed session finds the checkout it worked in; resume from a shell with the same `TMPDIR`. When that directory is still there (an unfinished cleanup, or another process holding the path), resume refuses before it starts: remove the directory, then resume. Resume uses the original attempt and does not spend another attempt quota. The default maximum is three resumes and 60 minutes of accumulated wall-clock; configure `resume.max_resumes`/`max_wall_time` to change these bounds. Policy changes, changed inputs, lost or rewritten predecessors, terminal predecessors and spent budgets refuse. An immutable predecessor claim permits only one continuation; repeated requests return the recorded result or expose its pending reservation without launching another process. A lost host before a result is published remains explicit incomplete evidence; this is not automatic recovery without a captured interrupted record.","numLines":1,"startLine":1045,"totalLines":1087}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jd1e2rgwDqdCDcn6t7xqsH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
