{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UQGh6DyTbTN5t7yeHWagUA","type":"tool_result","content":"907\tThe sandboxed Claude review profile that pose-dist qualified for its own reviews uses safe/restricted mode, Read/Grep/Glob/Bash only, mandatory shell sandboxing (`failIfUnavailable:true`, `allowUnsandboxedCommands:false`), and a read-only sealed source tree. Both fresh and resumed wrappers require bubblewrap, socat and jq on Linux (jq remains required on macOS), with installation advice on refusal. Go cache/temp writes go to private operation-owned scratch outside the checkout; the existing module cache is read, and unavailable downloads/tests that write into source can fail. The profile instructs the reviewer to run `go clean -cache` as its final Bash command inside the sandbox; the engine independently retains incomplete cleanup as a failed run under its unchanged limits. Never clean an adapter-controlled cache outside the sandbox: a test can replace its path with a symlink. This qualifies Claude's shell subprocess boundary, not isolation of the trusted Claude executable or arbitrary credential reads. Checkout integrity checks still apply. Installing engine code does not adopt the profile in another instance; copy and qualify its explicit policy block before use. The wrapper also denies the resolved physical Git common directory, because Claude auto-allows it for worktrees. For this opt-in profile, POSE prepares only empty `.claude/.cc-writes` directories at the disposable checkout root and declared components before taking its integrity snapshot; added files and all later mutations still fail. Final sandboxed cleanup includes leftover `go-build*` directories directly under GOTMPDIR after all jobs finish."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"ee597f18-b58a-4697-b866-359f1bde1d6a","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:19:23.499Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-r