{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KFzrpGHyZki2QUgFE6PZzB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"safety\": {\n3\t    \"schema_version\": 1,\n4\t    \"profile\": \"legacy-trusted\",\n5\t    \"platform\": \"linux/amd64\",\n6\t    \"capabilities\": {\n7\t      \"automatic-expiry\": \"unavailable\",\n8\t      \"bounded-capture\": \"available\",\n9\t      \"cpu-limit\": \"unavailable\",\n10\t      \"credential-filesystem-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n11\t      \"environment-allowlist\": \"available\",\n12\t      \"escaped-descendant-termination\": \"environment-marked\",\n13\t      \"filesystem-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n14\t      \"memory-limit\": \"unavailable\",\n15\t      \"network-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n16\t      \"origin-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n17\t      \"parent-termination\": \"available\",\n18\t      \"process-group-termination\": \"available\",\n19\t      \"shared-git-isolation\": \"unavailable\"\n20\t    },\n21\t    \"limitations\": [\n22\t      \"trusted local executable required; worktree is not a sandbox\",\n23\t      \"outside writes, transient writes, shared Git and credential files are not isolated\",\n24\t      \"no memory/CPU quota; the review run shim ends every process left in the run's subtree, including one in its own session\",\n25\t      \"cleanup filesystem calls remain subject to operating-system I/O latency\",\n26\t      \"legacy compatibility: HOME retained; other ambient credentials excluded\"\n27\t    ],\n28\t    \"stream_bytes\": 8388608,\n29\t    \"output_bytes\": 65536,\n30\t    \"retained_bytes\": 16777216,\n31\t    \"timeout_ms\": 3600000,\n32\t    \"max_runs_per_bundle\": 3,\n33\t    \"retention\": \"retain-evidence; ttl=0; no automatic deletion\",\n34\t    \"capture_complete\": true,\n35\t    \"runtime_id\": \"pose-review-run-93b9b9511d1567d3fc5c2c9979b76703\",\n36\t    \"operation\": {\n37\t      \"schema_version\": 1,\n38\t      \"operation\": \"review.dispatch.cleanup\",\n39\t      \"scope\": \"spec:pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\",\n40\t      \"outcome\": \"completed\",\n41\t      \"steps_run\": [\n42\t        {\n43\t          \"id\": \"cleanup\",\n44\t          \"result\": \"done\"\n45\t        }\n46\t      ],\n47\t      \"effects\": [],\n48\t      \"resumable\": false\n49\t    }\n50\t  },\n51\t  \"provenance\": {\n52\t    \"execution_state\": \"started\",\n53\t    \"planned_wire_digest\": \"sha256:0d28353bb8e8b76f8f5044a28946119d5bf3062096432bd32eb84bb7d5ba5299\",\n54\t    \"wire_bytes\": 29928,\n55\t    \"wire_complete\": true,\n56\t    \"schema_version\": 1,\n57\t    \"project\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n58\t    \"audience\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n59\t    \"worktree_digest\": \"sha256:092ca52378c4c0d0f2b627da8d5031dbb854563bd4b9f2474458710c62a14816\",\n60\t    \"trust\": \"executor-attested\",\n61\t    \"implementation\": {\n62\t      \"principal\": \"agent:anthropic/claude-opus-5-5\",\n63\t      \"execution\": \"sha256:344ac5868944c155772d60a95ef6ff20644580a642e772ad5c92c29428464ff8\",\n64\t      \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n65\t      \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n66\t    },\n67\t    \"reviewer\": {\n68\t      \"principal\": \"agent:anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n69\t      \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n70\t      \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\"\n71\t    },\n72\t    \"config_digest\": \"sha256:b23684d462090c30b29c472aa98a57bfadccc0b92e14fbacb173eb47d1f5b8ea\",\n73\t    \"command_template_digest\": \"sha256:3d843a49f6314194edbdf4f7f3ce02992895b45ad84d90915a0b66a1db8afd54\",\n74\t    \"argv_digest\": \"sha256:3299887be64211603f061d2b2b7ede0317c65f3b512cf206eba0578637fe909d\",\n75\t    \"executable_digest\": \"sha256:c157074818b094c84aaf31b8c80a1e149f234bb1c8c84a25e9a53e96afa30a29\",\n76\t    \"template_version\": \"review-brief/11\",\n77\t    \"wire_digest\": \"sha256:0d28353bb8e8b76f8f5044a28946119d5bf3062096432bd32eb84bb7d5ba5299\",\n78\t    \"notes_digest\": \"sha256:e1f35bc3ffc96a9ea534f0c623a3ec5e79a8e450ac94e05d7bf79ca9bda917e2\",\n79\t    \"raw_transcript_digest\": \"sha256:8c72581af06fe96bd42b7952ae9bbe0220e83d11e46e02531fc94bca54c6fd63\",\n80\t    \"raw_output_digest\": \"sha256:8cd8b1e731bc26e19a805da5d7458f33ea209c10f376cffd8bac50f1d6116447\",\n81\t    \"output_source\": \"stream-final\",\n82\t    \"output_complete\": true\n83\t  },\n84\t  \"session_digest\": \"sha256:df53332fe812ec9213b348544a855387ab8171eb86e87a8b5db30642389a15b1\",\n85\t  \"tree_digest\": \"sha256:a6e9e95c40d06420100ea7953d8b2105cb31c45b97142ca7aab534e47f8bc074\",\n86\t  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\nScope: spec `pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout` (R1–R3, decision D1, accepted limits L1–L2). On 2026-11-25 a `pose delegate resume` started a new run whose resumed Codex session still referred to the first attempt's sealed checkout, which the interrupted run's cleanup had removed; the reviewer stopped and the resume produced nothing.\\n- R1: every run of an attempt now uses the same runtime directory, `pose-review-run-\\u003cfirst 32 hex of the attempt id\\u003e` under the temporary directory (`reviewRunRuntimeDir` in `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go`), so the checkout is recreated at the path the session saw. A run without an attempt keeps a random name.\\n- R2: `TestResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath` (internal/cli) records the first run's working directory, checks it was removed, and resumes with an adapter that fails unless it runs there.\\n- R3: the directory is created with `os.Mkdir`; an existing path or a link fails the run with its reason (`TestTheAttemptRuntimeDirectoryIsCreatedExclusively`).\\nEach test fails with its guard mutated out. D1 explains why the path is kept stable instead of telling the session a new one (the continuation sends the sealed brief, whose wire digest provenance checks).\\n\\nPlease check in particular that no run can share or follow a directory it did not create, that cleanup still removes the whole runtime directory, and that runs outside an attempt behave as before.\\n\\nBefore you finish, run `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -` on your final message (pipe it on standard input) and fix every reason it reports.\\n\\nDraft format rules, enforced by the conclusion preflight:\\n- New findings use short unprefixed IDs (N1, N2, …).\\n- Structural-delta mappings go inside the criterion that answers them, with `basis` set to a requirement or a decision of this spec (R1–R3, D1).\\n- A criterion scoped to a component cites evidence from that component only.\\n- A finding that falls inside an accepted limit (L1, L2) is a follow-up with `limit` set to its id.\\n\\nSandbox limits: the checkout is sealed and read-only. Never `cd`; keep the checkout root as the working directory. Your Bash is limited to these command prefixes: `go test`, `go vet`, `go -C`, `git diff|log|show|status|ls-files`, `cat`, `printf`, `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\"`, and the pose checks the plan lists. Keep test runs focused (`go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'RunContinuity|ResumedReview|AttemptRuntimeDirectory'`, `go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose`), and let every command you start finish before you end. Run every planned `pose` command as `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\"`. A tool you cannot rerun in the sandbox is a limit of the run, not a defect of the subject: cite the sealed evidence that covers it.\\n\\nPlease report every finding you see in this round, classified blocker or follow-up, rather than stopping at the first.\\n\",\n87\t  \"ledger_version\": 1,\n88\t  \"attempt_id\": \"rat-93b9b9511d1567d3fc5c2c9979b76703f8e8f35ec49fd9596f1633ce89e187e6\",\n89\t  \"schema_version\": 1,\n90\t  \"run_id\": \"rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2\",\n91\t  \"scope\": \"spec:pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\",\n92\t  \"bundle_id\": \"rvb-5cd3a049a99eda9c\",\n93\t  \"bundle_digest\": \"sha256:5cd3a049a99eda9c1be73d35fcf09e4e58508efb6ac41164bc100e249940f76d\",\n94\t  \"sealed_commit\": \"e26623a150f5cdbe5c83366a6b12c30bc0f727ea\",\n95\t  \"kind\": \"review\",\n96\t  \"brief_digest\": \"sha256:f271b98a17e2aac186b32d0f76cf1d1c9922aa5d767853da9de8a09e9d94ec39\",\n97\t  \"adapter\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n98\t  \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n99\t  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n100\t  \"started_at\": \"2026-11-26T07:19:47.155835315Z\",\n101\t  \"ended_at\": \"2026-11-26T07:22:10.264528656Z\",\n102\t  \"exit_code\": 0,\n103\t  \"status\": \"completed\",\n104\t  \"transcript_digest\": \"sha256:51615193796db4e0e82ea0ba9a165b3ad73accbfcabda02bc87c8396719e79fb\",\n105\t  \"transcript_path\": \".pose/review-runs/rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2.transcript\",\n106\t  \"output\": \"**Review incomplete: I have not reached an approval or rejection.** The Bash sandbox failed on every call with `Sandbox is required but failed to initialize: Failed to create bridge sockets after 5 attempts. Restart to retry.` Overriding it isn't allowed.\\n\\n## What did not run\\n\\n- **Tests:** no `go test` or `go vet`, so I haven't checked the claim that each test fails when its guard is removed.\\n- **Diff:** no `git diff` or `git status`. I read the current files, so I haven't confirmed the change is limited to the three listed files.\\n- **Planned tools:** none of the `pose` tools ran, including the required `artifact-check`, which has no sealed evidence to stand in for it.\\n- **Draft check:** `review draft-check` did not run.\\n- **Cleanup failed:** `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal did not run. I started no builds or background jobs.\\n\\nI'm not including a `pose-draft` block. A complete one would need me to report required tools as passed when they never ran. Please rerun the review in a session where the sandbox starts.\\n\\n## Defects found by reading the code\\n\\nNone looks like a blocker. All are unconfirmed by execution.\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Location | Defect |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| N1 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:809` (claim at `:746`) | The directory is created after the predecessor has been claimed. If the path already exists, the interrupted run's one continuation becomes a failed, non-resumable run. Removing the directory doesn't restore `resume` on the original run, which returns the recorded failure; only a handoff or a new dispatch remains. The error at `:2052` gives no remedy. The spec's technical risk (line 73, \\\"fails until it is removed\\\") understates this. The blocking itself falls within L2 (or follows a leftover directory), but the lost resumability isn't stated there. |\\n| N2 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go:304` | `test -f .pose/specs/alpha/spec.md \\\\|\\\\| ls \\u003e\\u00262` can't fail the script, because a successful `ls` lets it continue to approval. The R2 test checks only that the working directory path matches, not that the checkout has content. |\\n| N3 | low | `POSE.md:1045` | The resume documentation doesn't say that the checkout path is now stable per attempt, that resume needs the same `TMPDIR` (L1), or what to do when the directory already exists. I didn't check the scaffold and locale copies for equivalent text. |\\n| N4 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:814-829` | If `Lstat` or `OpenRoot` fails right after the directory is created, `cleanup` is still nil. The run records cleanup as completed while the directory remains, and that now blocks later runs of the attempt. The misreport appears to predate this change; the blocking is new. It's unlikely to happen. |\\n| N5 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:2049` | A process that escaped an earlier run now knows the next run's paths, including `output.txt`. This matters mainly off Linux, where `reapSealedCheckoutProcesses` does nothing. Writes inside the worktree after the baseline snapshot would be detected, but `output.txt` sits outside it. Random names previously prevented this. |\\n\\n## Static assessment of the main questions\\n\\n- **No sharing or following:** `os.Mkdir` at `:2050` refuses an existing path, including a final-component link. Attempt IDs hash a random nonce (`review_attempt_ledger.go:427-432`), and continuations are claimed exclusively before the directory is created.\\n- **Cleanup:** on the normal path, `cleanupReviewResources` removes the worktree, its Git registration and then the runtime directory. This lets a resume add a worktree at the same path again. N4 is the exception I found.\\n- **Runs without an attempt:** they still use `os.MkdirTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"pose-review-run-*\\\")`.\\n- **Released abandoned attempts:** a leftover directory shouldn't newly block a handoff. The release record has no brief digest (`delegation_release.go:159-169`), so the handoff digest check should already refuse it.\\n- **Design (D1, R1, R3):** a stable path per attempt is a small change that addresses the stated cause without altering the sealed brief. It stops working if `TMPDIR` differs (L1). I found no reason to dispute L1 or L2 beyond the gap in N1.\\n- **Round-to-round session reuse:** a later round is a new attempt, so it gets a new path. The spec's goal covers only `delegate resume`, so I haven't counted this as a defect.\\n\\nThe sealed evidence listed in the brief reports passes, but I didn't re-verify any of it, and I'm not marking any criterion as passed.\",\n107\t  \"policy_digest\": \"sha256:96d45d57ca07ec9abf850150e8563fe243393ebd1604a49798920f6dade4dbe7\",\n108\t  \"label\": \"resume-review-r1\",\n109\t  \"purpose\": \"review\",\n110\t  \"env_removed\": [\n111\t    \"CLAUDECODE\",\n112\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_BRIDGE_SESSION_ID\",\n113\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION\",\n114\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT\",\n115\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH\",\n116\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET\",\n117\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_TOKEN\",\n118\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ATTENDED\",\n119\t    \"CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID\",\n120\t    \"CLAUDE_EFFORT\",\n121\t    \"CLAUDE_PID\"\n122\t  ],\n123\t  \"events\": \"claude-stream-json\",\n124\t  \"events_digest\": \"sha256:beaa0c723697e4d456569ea945af5a5604d4da174596316ce07d0bd96a9f2d29\",\n125\t  \"routing\": {\n126\t    \"requested\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n127\t    \"implementation\": {\n128\t      \"principal\": \"agent:anthropic/claude-opus-5-5\",\n129\t      \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n130\t      \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\",\n131\t      \"execution_digest\": \"sha256:344ac5868944c155772d60a95ef6ff20644580a642e772ad5c92c29428464ff8\",\n132\t      \"source\": \"declared\"\n133\t    },\n134\t    \"implementation_from\": \"bundle\",\n135\t    \"step\": \"explicit\"\n136\t  },\n137\t  \"independence_achieved\": \"different-model\",\n138\t  \"round\": 1\n139\t}\n140\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"1ef15684-64ed-4c84-8190-f60ae6fdebfa","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:19:30.246Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-ed41371fa91497af9df96f254af372d5/worktree/.pose/review-runs/rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2.json","content":"{\n  \"safety\": {\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"profile\": \"legacy-trusted\",\n    \"platform\": \"linux/amd64\",\n    \"capabilities\": {\n      \"automatic-expiry\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"bounded-capture\": \"available\",\n      \"cpu-limit\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"credential-filesystem-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"environment-allowlist\": \"available\",\n      \"escaped-descendant-termination\": \"environment-marked\",\n      \"filesystem-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"memory-limit\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"network-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"origin-isolation\": \"unavailable\",\n      \"parent-termination\": \"available\",\n      \"process-group-termination\": \"available\",\n      \"shared-git-isolation\": \"unavailable\"\n    },\n    \"limitations\": [\n      \"trusted local executable required; worktree is not a sandbox\",\n      \"outside writes, transient writes, shared Git and credential files are not isolated\",\n      \"no memory/CPU quota; the review run shim ends every process left in the run's subtree, including one in its own session\",\n      \"cleanup filesystem calls remain subject to operating-system I/O latency\",\n      \"legacy compatibility: HOME retained; other ambient credentials excluded\"\n    ],\n    \"stream_bytes\": 8388608,\n    \"output_bytes\": 65536,\n    \"retained_bytes\": 16777216,\n    \"timeout_ms\": 3600000,\n    \"max_runs_per_bundle\": 3,\n    \"retention\": \"retain-evidence; ttl=0; no automatic deletion\",\n    \"capture_complete\": true,\n    \"runtime_id\": \"pose-review-run-93b9b9511d1567d3fc5c2c9979b76703\",\n    \"operation\": {\n      \"schema_version\": 1,\n      \"operation\": \"review.dispatch.cleanup\",\n      \"scope\": \"spec:pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\",\n      \"outcome\": \"completed\",\n      \"steps_run\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"cleanup\",\n          \"result\": \"done\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"effects\": [],\n      \"resumable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"execution_state\": \"started\",\n    \"planned_wire_digest\": \"sha256:0d28353bb8e8b76f8f5044a28946119d5bf3062096432bd32eb84bb7d5ba5299\",\n    \"wire_bytes\": 29928,\n    \"wire_complete\": true,\n    \"schema_version\": 1,\n    \"project\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n    \"audience\": \"proj.pose-dist\",\n    \"worktree_digest\": \"sha256:092ca52378c4c0d0f2b627da8d5031dbb854563bd4b9f2474458710c62a14816\",\n    \"trust\": \"executor-attested\",\n    \"implementation\": {\n      \"principal\": \"agent:anthropic/claude-opus-5-5\",\n      \"execution\": \"sha256:344ac5868944c155772d60a95ef6ff20644580a642e772ad5c92c29428464ff8\",\n      \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"model\": \"claude-opus-5-5\"\n    },\n    \"reviewer\": {\n      \"principal\": \"agent:anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n      \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\"\n    },\n    \"config_digest\": \"sha256:b23684d462090c30b29c472aa98a57bfadccc0b92e14fbacb173eb47d1f5b8ea\",\n    \"command_template_digest\": \"sha256:3d843a49f6314194edbdf4f7f3ce02992895b45ad84d90915a0b66a1db8afd54\",\n    \"argv_digest\": \"sha256:3299887be64211603f061d2b2b7ede0317c65f3b512cf206eba0578637fe909d\",\n    \"executable_digest\": \"sha256:c157074818b094c84aaf31b8c80a1e149f234bb1c8c84a25e9a53e96afa30a29\",\n    \"template_version\": \"review-brief/11\",\n    \"wire_digest\": \"sha256:0d28353bb8e8b76f8f5044a28946119d5bf3062096432bd32eb84bb7d5ba5299\",\n    \"notes_digest\": \"sha256:e1f35bc3ffc96a9ea534f0c623a3ec5e79a8e450ac94e05d7bf79ca9bda917e2\",\n    \"raw_transcript_digest\": \"sha256:8c72581af06fe96bd42b7952ae9bbe0220e83d11e46e02531fc94bca54c6fd63\",\n    \"raw_output_digest\": \"sha256:8cd8b1e731bc26e19a805da5d7458f33ea209c10f376cffd8bac50f1d6116447\",\n    \"output_source\": \"stream-final\",\n    \"output_complete\": true\n  },\n  \"session_digest\": \"sha256:df53332fe812ec9213b348544a855387ab8171eb86e87a8b5db30642389a15b1\",\n  \"tree_digest\": \"sha256:a6e9e95c40d06420100ea7953d8b2105cb31c45b97142ca7aab534e47f8bc074\",\n  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\nScope: spec `pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout` (R1–R3, decision D1, accepted limits L1–L2). On 2026-11-25 a `pose delegate resume` started a new run whose resumed Codex session still referred to the first attempt's sealed checkout, which the interrupted run's cleanup had removed; the reviewer stopped and the resume produced nothing.\\n- R1: every run of an attempt now uses the same runtime directory, `pose-review-run-\\u003cfirst 32 hex of the attempt id\\u003e` under the temporary directory (`reviewRunRuntimeDir` in `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go`), so the checkout is recreated at the path the session saw. A run without an attempt keeps a random name.\\n- R2: `TestResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath` (internal/cli) records the first run's working directory, checks it was removed, and resumes with an adapter that fails unless it runs there.\\n- R3: the directory is created with `os.Mkdir`; an existing path or a link fails the run with its reason (`TestTheAttemptRuntimeDirectoryIsCreatedExclusively`).\\nEach test fails with its guard mutated out. D1 explains why the path is kept stable instead of telling the session a new one (the continuation sends the sealed brief, whose wire digest provenance checks).\\n\\nPlease check in particular that no run can share or follow a directory it did not create, that cleanup still removes the whole runtime directory, and that runs outside an attempt behave as before.\\n\\nBefore you finish, run `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -` on your final message (pipe it on standard input) and fix every reason it reports.\\n\\nDraft format rules, enforced by the conclusion preflight:\\n- New findings use short unprefixed IDs (N1, N2, …).\\n- Structural-delta mappings go inside the criterion that answers them, with `basis` set to a requirement or a decision of this spec (R1–R3, D1).\\n- A criterion scoped to a component cites evidence from that component only.\\n- A finding that falls inside an accepted limit (L1, L2) is a follow-up with `limit` set to its id.\\n\\nSandbox limits: the checkout is sealed and read-only. Never `cd`; keep the checkout root as the working directory. Your Bash is limited to these command prefixes: `go test`, `go vet`, `go -C`, `git diff|log|show|status|ls-files`, `cat`, `printf`, `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\"`, and the pose checks the plan lists. Keep test runs focused (`go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'RunContinuity|ResumedReview|AttemptRuntimeDirectory'`, `go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose`), and let every command you start finish before you end. Run every planned `pose` command as `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\"`. A tool you cannot rerun in the sandbox is a limit of the run, not a defect of the subject: cite the sealed evidence that covers it.\\n\\nPlease report every finding you see in this round, classified blocker or follow-up, rather than stopping at the first.\\n\",\n  \"ledger_version\": 1,\n  \"attempt_id\": \"rat-93b9b9511d1567d3fc5c2c9979b76703f8e8f35ec49fd9596f1633ce89e187e6\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"run_id\": \"rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2\",\n  \"scope\": \"spec:pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout\",\n  \"bundle_id\": \"rvb-5cd3a049a99eda9c\",\n  \"bundle_digest\": \"sha256:5cd3a049a99eda9c1be73d35fcf09e4e58508efb6ac41164bc100e249940f76d\",\n  \"sealed_commit\": \"e26623a150f5cdbe5c83366a6b12c30bc0f727ea\",\n  \"kind\": \"review\",\n  \"brief_digest\": \"sha256:f271b98a17e2aac186b32d0f76cf1d1c9922aa5d767853da9de8a09e9d94ec39\",\n  \"adapter\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n  \"vendor\": \"anthropic\",\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-11-26T07:19:47.155835315Z\",\n  \"ended_at\": \"2026-11-26T07:22:10.264528656Z\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"transcript_digest\": \"sha256:51615193796db4e0e82ea0ba9a165b3ad73accbfcabda02bc87c8396719e79fb\",\n  \"transcript_path\": \".pose/review-runs/rrn-7adbffa551b9acf2.transcript\",\n  \"output\": \"**Review incomplete: I have not reached an approval or rejection.** The Bash sandbox failed on every call with `Sandbox is required but failed to initialize: Failed to create bridge sockets after 5 attempts. Restart to retry.` Overriding it isn't allowed.\\n\\n## What did not run\\n\\n- **Tests:** no `go test` or `go vet`, so I haven't checked the claim that each test fails when its guard is removed.\\n- **Diff:** no `git diff` or `git status`. I read the current files, so I haven't confirmed the change is limited to the three listed files.\\n- **Planned tools:** none of the `pose` tools ran, including the required `artifact-check`, which has no sealed evidence to stand in for it.\\n- **Draft check:** `review draft-check` did not run.\\n- **Cleanup failed:** `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal did not run. I started no builds or background jobs.\\n\\nI'm not including a `pose-draft` block. A complete one would need me to report required tools as passed when they never ran. Please rerun the review in a session where the sandbox starts.\\n\\n## Defects found by reading the code\\n\\nNone looks like a blocker. All are unconfirmed by execution.\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Location | Defect |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| N1 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:809` (claim at `:746`) | The directory is created after the predecessor has been claimed. If the path already exists, the interrupted run's one continuation becomes a failed, non-resumable run. Removing the directory doesn't restore `resume` on the original run, which returns the recorded failure; only a handoff or a new dispatch remains. The error at `:2052` gives no remedy. The spec's technical risk (line 73, \\\"fails until it is removed\\\") understates this. The blocking itself falls within L2 (or follows a leftover directory), but the lost resumability isn't stated there. |\\n| N2 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go:304` | `test -f .pose/specs/alpha/spec.md \\\\|\\\\| ls \\u003e\\u00262` can't fail the script, because a successful `ls` lets it continue to approval. The R2 test checks only that the working directory path matches, not that the checkout has content. |\\n| N3 | low | `POSE.md:1045` | The resume documentation doesn't say that the checkout path is now stable per attempt, that resume needs the same `TMPDIR` (L1), or what to do when the directory already exists. I didn't check the scaffold and locale copies for equivalent text. |\\n| N4 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:814-829` | If `Lstat` or `OpenRoot` fails right after the directory is created, `cleanup` is still nil. The run records cleanup as completed while the directory remains, and that now blocks later runs of the attempt. The misreport appears to predate this change; the blocking is new. It's unlikely to happen. |\\n| N5 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:2049` | A process that escaped an earlier run now knows the next run's paths, including `output.txt`. This matters mainly off Linux, where `reapSealedCheckoutProcesses` does nothing. Writes inside the worktree after the baseline snapshot would be detected, but `output.txt` sits outside it. Random names previously prevented this. |\\n\\n## Static assessment of the main questions\\n\\n- **No sharing or following:** `os.Mkdir` at `:2050` refuses an existing path, including a final-component link. Attempt IDs hash a random nonce (`review_attempt_ledger.go:427-432`), and continuations are claimed exclusively before the directory is created.\\n- **Cleanup:** on the normal path, `cleanupReviewResources` removes the worktree, its Git registration and then the runtime directory. This lets a resume add a worktree at the same path again. N4 is the exception I found.\\n- **Runs without an attempt:** they still use `os.MkdirTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"pose-review-run-*\\\")`.\\n- **Released abandoned attempts:** a leftover directory shouldn't newly block a handoff. The release record has no brief digest (`delegation_release.go:159-169`), so the handoff digest check should already refuse it.\\n- **Design (D1, R1, R3):** a stable path per attempt is a small change that addresses the stated cause without altering the sealed brief. It stops working if `TMPDIR` differs (L1). I found no reason to dispute L1 or L2 beyond the gap in N1.\\n- **Round-to-round session reuse:** a later round is a new attempt, so it gets a new path. The spec's goal covers only `delegate resume`, so I haven't counted this as a defect.\\n\\nThe sealed evidence listed in the brief reports passes, but I didn't re-verify any of it, and I'm not marking any criterion as 